===Etymology===
{{PIE root|gem-pro|h₁lewdʰ}}
From {{etyl|enm|en}} {{m|enm|leod||people}}, from {{etyl|ang|en}} {{m|ang|lēode}} {{gloss|"people, men"; plural of {{m|ang|lēod||person, man}}}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|en}} {{m|gem-pro|*liudiz|*liudīz|people}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|en}} {{m|ine-pro|*h₁lewdʰ-||man, people}}. Cognate with {{cog|sco|lede||people}}, {{cog|fy|lie||people}}, {{cog|nl|lieden||people}} and {{cog|nl|lui|lui(den)|people}}, {{cog|de|Leute||people}}, {{cog|no|lyd||people}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{enPR|lēd|lē-ōd}}, {{IPA|/liːd/|/liːod/|lang=en}}
* {{homophones|lang=en|lead}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|leod|leods}}

# {{form of|Alternative or obsolete form|lede|lang=en}}.
# {{lb|en|collectively|obsolete}} [[people|People]].
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} A [[people]], [[nation]], people group.
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} A [[man]], [[person]].

